<title>USA: Blessings ends payout, to buy back shares.</title>
<headline>Blessings ends payout, to buy back shares.</headline>
<dateline>NEWPORT NEWS, Va. 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Blessings Corp said it will buy back up to one million shares of common stock in a expanded buyback program and will no longer pay a regularly quarterly dividend.</p>
<p>The company's board decided against the dividend of $0.10 per share because &quot;significant investment opportunities are available to the company which should enhance shareholder value more effectively than cash dividend payments,&quot; according to Chairman John McMackin.</p>
<p>The company had paid a regular quarterly dividend of $0.10 per share.</p>
<p>The company said it would buy back the shares in the open market or in private transactions when it deemed appropriate.</p>
</text>
